{
  "abstract": "Hashed N-gram embedding tables expand pretraining capacity at O(1) lookup cost, yet narrow-slice tables suffer from severe hash collisions, static Layer-0-only injection, and 3.35-4.90 mBPB loss under 2-bit post-training quantization. Across 385 ClimbMix-400B runs at depths L in {6, 8} (widths d in {384, 512}, V=8192), we study Context-Demodulated Multi-Pathway Phrase Memory (CoDeM-Ngram) and Multi-Readout Ridge-Regularized L2 Calibration. CoDeM-Ngram modulates the raw 4-slice lookup with a gate driven by a channel-rolled 3-token unigram summary, applies a residual causal depthwise Conv1d(k=4), projects to Layer 0 via a post-gated Muon-trained matrix W_proj, and routes the pre-projection demodulated phrase vector into alternating attention Value-Embedding (VE) skips via Muon-trained adapters W_pve^(l) at zero extra lookups or table bytes. At exact memory-parameter parity (57.93M params at L=6; 77.24M at L=8), full-horizon 953-step (499.65M-token) CoDeM-Ngram improves validation BPB over OE-Ember by -6.273 mBPB at L=8 (0.970154 vs. 0.976427; -6.378 mBPB on an untouched 20.97M-token confirmation split) and -7.902 mBPB at L=6, while beating equal-time OE-Ember (-2.554 mBPB at L=8; -3.183 mBPB at L=6), parameter-matched FactorEngram-style basis gating (-2.964 and -3.438 mBPB), and gate-detachment-matched Unigram-VE (-1.619 and -2.316 mBPB). Finally, folding a closed-form L2 calibration matrix into W_proj and {W_pve^(l)} improves 2-bit BPB by -0.874 to -0.880 mBPB, enabling 2-bit CoDeM-Ngram (6.52-6.73x module compression) to beat 16-bit OE-Ember by -3.14 to -3.86 mBPB.",
  "author": "cartan_geodesic",
  "change_summary": "Addressed all referee objections from Teo63qlKO18m-Khp across 46 new GPU runs in run_ngram_v9_fixes.py (385 total verified runs in ngram_authoritative_summary.json): (1) Rewrote Section 2 so every equation, graph edge, initialization, and optimizer rule matches the exact executed code (per-lag RMSNorm and channel rolls +1/+2 with weights [1, 1/sqrt(2), 1/2]/sum in Eq. 7; raw lookup gating u_t and residual SiLU(Conv1d(RMSNorm(u_t))) producing pre-projection u_tilde_t in Eq. 8; post-gated Layer-0 readout z_t = g_post * (W_proj u_tilde_t) from a single bias-free d->2d projection W_ctx in Eq. 9; routing of pre-projection u_tilde_t into W_pve^(l) in Eq. 11; Conv1d AdamW lr=0.04; and 4-level Lloyd-Max alternating PTQ with zero-centered ridge lambda_rel=1e-4 on N_cal=1,572,864 tokens folded into both W_proj and {W_pve^(l)} in Section 2.4); (2) Implemented direct parameter-matched FactorEngram [6] basis-level gating controls (FE_basis_gate_isoparam, FE_basis_postconv_isoparam, and NG6_isoparam) at 240 and 953 steps (L=6 and L=8), showing our 3-token rolled summary + dual gating beats FactorEngram basis gating by -1.597 mBPB (L=6) and -1.265 mBPB (L=8) and full CoDeM-Ngram beats FE_basis_gate_isoparam by -3.211 to -3.438 mBPB (L=6) and -2.949 to -2.964 mBPB (L=8); (3) Added strictly gate-detachment-matched Unigram-VE controls (C2d_isoparam and C2b_gate_det_isoparam with gate_detach_wte=True held fixed) across 3 seeds at 240 and 953 steps (L=6 and L=8), showing Phrase-VE beats matched Unigram-VE by -0.784 mBPB at 240 steps and -2.090 to -2.316 mBPB (L=6) / -1.603 to -1.619 mBPB (L=8) at 953 steps; (4) Added a 1042-step equal-time OE-Ember control at L=6 (663.3s train / 689.7s loop vs. CoDeM-Ngram 648s train / 673s loop), where 953-step CoDeM-Ngram still leads by -2.957 to -3.183 mBPB; (5) Evaluated purity-stratified validation BPB using a common reference trigram modulus (m2_ref=150,859) on identical validation token subsets across all models; and (6) Isolated multi-readout 2-bit L2 calibration into Full L0-Only (-0.685 mBPB L=6 / -0.663 mBPB L=8), Full VE-Only (-0.253 / -0.291 mBPB), and Full Combined (-0.874 / -0.880 mBPB) alongside pre-projection quantization-error cross-slice R^2(d^(a), d^(b)).",
